---
title: Thin Milk Chocolate Ganache
yield: 300%g
---

= Preparation

Ensure the assembled cake (Sponge, Crunch, and Mousse) is frozen solid and level in its #cake frame{} before starting.

= Heat the Liquids

Combine @heavy cream{100%ml} and @glucose syrup{15%g} in a #small saucepan{}. 

Heat over medium heat until it reaches a gentle simmer, approximately 80°C. Do not let it reach a rolling boil.

= The Emulsion

Place @milk chocolate{150%g}(finely chopped) in a #heat-proof bowl{}. 

Pour the hot cream mixture over the chocolate and let it sit undisturbed for ~{60%seconds} to melt.

Using a #small whisk{} or #spatula{}, stir in small circles starting from the center and gradually widening until the mixture is glossy and emulsified.

= Adding Gloss

Once the ganache has cooled to 40°C, stir in the cubed @butter{20%g} until completely melted and smooth. 

For a glass-like finish, use an #immersion blender{} at low speed, keeping it fully submerged to avoid air bubbles.

= The Pour

When the ganache reaches 30°C to 32°C, pour it into the center of the frozen cake. 

Quickly tilt the #tray{} in all directions to allow the ganache to run evenly to the edges.

= Setting

Place the cake in the #fridge{} for ~{30%minutes} to set the glaze, then move it to the #freezer{} for ~{2%hours} before final trimming and slicing.